WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.840
On the first Sunday of Lent, Orthodox
Christians celebrate the Sunday of Orthodoxy.

2
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:11.210
It remembers the year 843, when icons
were restored after emperors had ordered

3
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.560
them removed.

4
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:18.480
Centuries later, in 1524, the churches
of Zurich removed their images.

5
00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.610
So why do some Christians
kiss a painted picture,

6
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.950
while others say it breaks
the Ten Commandments?

7
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.850
In this mission, you'll
learn to read an icon:

8
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.650
its gold background, its missing shadows,

9
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.460
its large eyes.

10
00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.030
Then you'll read the
commandment against images,

11
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.570
and see where different churches stand.

12
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: explain why one painted
picture can divide Christians so sharply.
